VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it to 0.8 to 5 on a Tuesday afternoon. Flagged volume drops. The review queue shortens. And the model is bite forbite identical. Neither change looks like a change. Now that number I asked you to'

[10:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hold on to, base ministral 3B before any safety training scored zero on F1 because it never predicted a violation. Not once, 0% recall. It said safe to everything. And on that same evaluation,'

[10:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it still posted an accuracy figure of 37.8%. Because most content genuinely is safe. A completely broken gate and a well-tuned one produce the same shape of'

[10:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'dashboard, a low unsafe rate. If the only thing you report upward is flagged volume, you cannot distinguish a model that\'s working from a model answering no to everything. That\'s the governance problem in one line. You cannot tell'

[10:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'whether your flag rate fell because the product got cleaner, because someone edited a sentence, or because the gate stopped working. In my experience, that ambiguity is where the real failures'

[11:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'live. Not in the control being absent, in the control being present, reporting a healthy number, and nobody being able to say who last changed what it measures. The fix isn\'t technical, and it isn\'t expensive. Three habits. Almost'

[11:22] [scene:talk]
