[12:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hardware and this one is short. 3 billion parameters, multimodal, 32,000 token context at half precision. That\'s roughly 6 GB of weights. Mistral quotes 16 GB to leave room for the vision'

[13:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'encoder and the cache. RTX 590 32 GB go comfortably at full precision with room to batch. Mac Studio Ultra 256 GB go. Capacity isn\'t remotely the constraint.'

[13:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'The barrier here was never the hardware. If your organization runs any kind of content moderation, three questions are worth asking this week. One, who wrote the policy question and where is that'

[13:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wording stored and versioned? Two, who can change the threshold and does that change get logged with a name against it? Three, if your flag content rate moved last quarter, can you tell whether'

[13:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the product changed, the setting changed, or the gate stopped working? If the answer to the third one is no, the first two are why. The verdict here leans toward promise and it isn\'t close.'

[13:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'A capability that costs money and required shipping your users\'s content to somebody else\'s servers is now free, open, and running on a machine under a desk. Data residency shops get an option'

[14:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'they did not have last week. Anyone running a model at home gets a filter on the inbound side for nothing. That\'s a real game. The catch is the one you attach yourself. A control you rent comes with somebody else\'s defaults,'

[14:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'somebody else\'s taxonomy, and somebody else\'s audit trail. A control you own comes with none of them, which is exactly what you wanted and exactly what you now have to maintain. Free is the right price. Ownership is the actual'

